s","issue-tracking"]}],"skills":[{"path":".claude/skills/auditing-upstream-drift/SKILL.md","name":"auditing-upstream-drift","description":"Use when checking if beads-superpowers is outdated, before a plugin release, or when auditing for missing capabilities — covers upstream drift, test execution, documentation, plugin health, and content integrity","headings":["Auditing Upstream Drift","When to Use","Upstream Sources","Known Deliberate Divergences","The Audit Process","Phase 4: Progressive Skill Chain Integrity","brainstorming → writing-plans (terminal state)","writing-plans → subagent-driven-development OR executing-plans","subagent-driven-development → finishing-a-development-branch","executing-plans → finishing-a-development-branch","finishing-a-development-branch has Land the Plane","using-superpowers has ## Beads section","verification-before-completion has Beads Completion section","Phase 5: Upstream Superpowers Drift","Lines starting with < are skills upstream has that we don't","Phase 6: Upstream Beads Drift","Compare against our baseline (v1.1.0)","Look for new commands not in our skills' Quick Reference tables"],"name_hint":"auditing · upstream · drift","description_zh":"检查 beads-superpowers 与上游的差异或缺失能力，用于插件发布前审计，涵盖测试、文档、插件健康及内容完整性。"},{"path":"skills/brainstorming/SKILL.md","name":"brainstorming","description":"You MUST use this before any creative work - creating features, building components, adding functionality, or modifying behavior. Explores user intent, requirements and design before implementation.","headings":["Brainstorming Ideas Into Designs","Anti-Pattern: \"This Is Too Simple To Need A Design\"","Checklist","Process Flow","The Process","After the Design","Open in user's preferred editor, with platform fallbacks","If none available: just report the path","Visual Companion","Integration"],"name_hint":"brainstorming","description_zh":"在新增功能、组件或修改行为前探索用户意图、需求和设计，先开展头脑风暴再实施。"},{"path":"skills/dispatching-parallel-agents/SKILL.md","name":"dispatching-parallel-agents","description":"Use when facing 2+ independent tasks that can be worked on without shared state or sequential dependencies","headings":["Dispatching Parallel Agents","Overview","When to Use","The Pattern","1. Identify Independent Domains","Before you fan out (orchestrator-only)","2. Create Focused Agent Tasks","3. Dispatch in Parallel","4. Review and Integrate","Agent Prompt Structure","Common Mistakes","When NOT to Use","Integration","SDD Integration","Real Example from Session","Verification"],"name_hint":"dispatching · parallel · 智能体","description_zh":"将两个及以上没有共享状态或顺序依赖的独立任务分派给并行智能体。"},{"path":"skills/document-release/SKILL.md","name":"document-release","description":"Use when implementation on a branch is complete and it is about to be merged or PR'd — or when finishing-a-development-branch reaches its docs-audit gate — and after code changes are committed, to ensure all project documentation accurately reflects shipped code. Covers README, ARCHITECTURE, CONTRIBUTING, CHANGELOG, CLAUDE.md, TODOS, and VERSION files. Triggers on \"update docs\", \"sync documentation\", \"post-ship docs\", \"document release\", \"documentation audit\".","headings":["Document Release: Post-Ship Documentation Update","Beads Integration","Create a doc-update bead at start","Key Operating Principles","Audit Methodology (9-Step Process)","Step 0: Platform Detection","Step 1: Pre-flight and Diff Analysis","Step 1.5: Coverage Map (Diataxis Blast-Radius Audit)","Step 2: Per-File Documentation Audit","Step 3: Apply Auto-Updates","Step 4: Ask About Risky Changes","Step 5: CHANGELOG Voice Polish","Step 6: Cross-Doc Consistency","Step 7: TODOS Cleanup","Step 8: VERSION Bump Decision","Step 9: Commit and Output","Critical Rules","Integration"],"name_hint":"文档 · release","description_zh":"在分支实现完成、代码已提交并准备合并或创建拉取请求时，审计并同步项目文档与实际发布代码，涵盖 README、ARCHITECTURE、CONTRIBUTING、CHANGELOG、CLAUDE.md、TODOS 和 VERSION。"},{"path":"skills/executing-plans/SKILL.md","name":"executing-plans","description":"Use when you have a written implementation plan to execute in a separate session with review checkpoints","headings":["Executing Plans","Overview","The Process","Step 1: Load and Review Plan","Success Criteria","Step 2: Execute Tasks","Step 3: Complete Development","When to Stop and Ask for Help","When to Revisit Earlier Steps","Remember"],"name_hint":"executing · plans","description_zh":"在独立会话中执行既有书面实施计划，并在检查点开展复核。"},{"path":"skills/finishing-a-development-branch/SKILL.md","name":"finishing-a-development-branch","description":"Use when implementation is complete, all tests pass, and you need to decide how to integrate the work - guides completion of development work by presenting structured options for merge, PR, or cleanup","headings":["Finishing a Development Branch","Overview","The Process","Step 1: Verify Tests","Run project's test suite","Check for duplicate beads (clean up before merge)","Step 2: Detect Environment","Capture now, while still inside the workspace — Step 5 changes directory","before Step 6 needs this value","Step 3: Determine Base Branch","Try common base branches","Step 3.5: Docs-Audit Gate","Step 4: Present Options","Step 5: Execute Choice","Leave the worktree first — checkout, merge, and worktree removal all have to","run from the main repo root, and Step 6 needs the path captured in Step 2","Merge first — verify the merged result before removing anything","Verify tests on merged result"],"name_hint":"finishing · a · development · 分支","description_zh":"在实现完成且测试通过后，提供合并、PR 或清理等结构化选项，帮助完成开发分支集成。"},{"path":"skills/getting-up-to-speed/SKILL.md","name":"getting-up-to-speed","description":"Orients on an unfamiliar or stale codebase at the start of a session, after compaction, or whenever the project state is unclear. Loads beads context, deep-dives the codebase, and produces a structured 'current state' summary. Triggers on phrases like \"catch me up\", \"where are we\", \"orient me\", \"what's the state of this project\", \"bring me up to speed\", \"load context\", \"session orientation\".","headings":["Getting Up to Speed","Steps","1 — Gather (at most 2 tool calls)","2 — Explore (one parallel batch — never serialize)","3 — Drill (bounded)","4 — Close","5 — Synthesize through the gate","What `<project>` Is","Architecture Highlights","Repo Layout (verified)","Current State","Recent Activity","Terminal contract","Red flags","Edge cases","Integration"],"name_hint":"getting · up · to · speed","description_zh":"在会话开始、上下文压缩后或项目状态不明时熟悉陌生或久未处理的代码库，加载 beads 上下文、深入代码并输出结构化的当前状态摘要。"},{"path":"skills/memory-curator/SKILL.md","name":"memory-curator","description":"Use at session-close when a session captured several new memories, or on-demand, to consolidate, deduplicate, prune, and structure the beads memory store. Triggers on \"curate memories\", \"clean up memories\", \"memory sweep\".","headings":["Memory Curator","When to Use","When NOT to Use","Memory taxonomy","Memory header","Beads-native knowledge store","The sweep","Iron rule: propose, then apply","Red Flags","Beads Integration","after the user approved + you applied:","Integration"],"name_hint":"记忆 · curator","description_zh":"在会话结束且新增了多条记忆时，或按需整理 beads 记忆库，进行合并、去重、删减和结构化。"},{"path":"skills/project-init/SKILL.md","name":"project-init","description":"Use when beads/Dolt database initialization fails, when bd commands return errors about missing databases, when setting up beads in a new project, or when recovering from diverged Dolt history. Handles fresh init, bootstrap from remote, and recovery workflows.","headings":["Project Init: Beads/Dolt Database Setup and Recovery","Iron Law: NEVER Run `bd init --force`","Diagnostic Phase (Always Run First)","Decision Matrix","Path A: Fresh Initialization (New Project)","1. Initialize beads","2. Verify","3. Add remote (if syncing) — RECOMMENDED: a dedicated beads remote (private for public projects),","separate from the code repo (ADR-0057; bd releases after v1.1.0 refuse a code-repo URL without --allow-git-origin)","4. First push","Path B: Bootstrap from Remote (Cloned Repo)","1. Bootstrap (auto-detects remote dolt data)","2. Verify","After any pull: repair denormalized blocked flags (bd v1.1.0+)","Path C: Fix Diverged History","Path D: Database Exists but Broken","1. Run doctor (non-destructive diagnostics + auto-fix)","2. If doctor fixes it:"],"name_hint":"项目 · init","description_zh":"处理 beads/Dolt 初始化失败、bd 缺少数据库、新项目接入及 Dolt 历史分叉问题，提供新建、从远端引导和恢复流程。"},{"path":"skills/receiving-code-review/SKILL.md","name":"receiving-code-review","description":"Use when receiving code review feedback, before implementing suggestions, especially if feedback seems unclear or technically questionable - requires technical rigor and verification, not performative agreement or blind implementation","headings":["Code Review Reception","Overview","The Response Pattern","Forbidden Responses","Handling Unclear Feedback","Source-Specific Handling","From your human partner","From External Reviewers","YAGNI Check for \"Professional\" Features","Implementation Order","When To Push Back","Acknowledging Correct Feedback","Gracefully Correcting Your Pushback","Common Mistakes","Real Examples","GitHub Thread Replies","Integration"],"name_hint":"receiving · 代码 · 评审","description_zh":"接收代码审查意见后先核验技术依据，尤其针对不清楚或可疑建议，避免未经验证直接修改。"},{"path":"skills/requesting-code-review/SKILL.md","name":"requesting-code-review","description":"Use when completing tasks, implementing major features, or before merging to verify work meets requirements","headings":["Requesting Code Review","When to Request Review","How to Request","Example","Integration","Common Rationalizations","Red Flags"],"name_hint":"requesting · 代码 · 评审","description_zh":"在任务或重大功能完成、合并前请求代码审查，核对变更是否满足需求。"},{"path":"skills/research-driven-development/SKILL.md","name":"research-driven-development","description":"Use when the user asks a question about a topic, requests research, or when understanding something is needed before planning. Triggers on \"research this\", \"what is X\", \"how does Y work\", \"compare A vs B\", \"investigate\", \"deep dive\", \"look into\".","headings":["Research-Driven Development","When to Use","When NOT to Use","Iron Law","Grounding Rule","Pipeline","Step 0: Scope Check (conditional)","Step 1: Create a Bead + Calibrate Effort","Step 2: Check Existing Knowledge","Check beads memories for prior context","Query the knowledge-beads — the primary dedup index now (reference-class","research lives here as deferred `research`-labeled beads, not in the old","kv store or as a doc-grep)","Step 3: Decompose + Dispatch Parallel Research Agents","The delegation contract (every dispatch)","Agent A: Researchers (web + documentation)","Agent B: @explore (codebase) — one agent, conditional","Step 4: Synthesize + Verify Findings"],"name_hint":"研究 · driven · development","description_zh":"在回答主题问题、开展研究或规划前需要理解背景时，进行资料研究、原理解释、方案比较或深入调查。"},{"path":"skills/session-handoff/SKILL.md","name":"session-handoff","description":"A human-invoked utility that writes a grounded session-handoff document (plus a continuation pointer memory) so a fresh agent can resume in-progress work. Not auto-invoked; a human runs it deliberately.","headings":["Session Handoff","When a human uses this","Pipeline","Doctrine","Red Flags (low-independence backstop — not the primary guard)","Integration"],"name_hint":"session · 交接","description_zh":"由用户主动调用，编写有事实依据的会话交接文档与继续执行指针记忆，使新代理能接续未完成的工作；不自动触发。"},{"path":"skills/stress-test/SKILL.md","name":"stress-test","description":"Use when a design, plan, or decision needs adversarial scrutiny before proceeding. Interrogates every branch of the decision tree, providing recommended answers and forcing explicit agreement or pushback. Triggers on \"grill me\", \"stress test this\", \"poke holes\", \"challenge this design\", or when brainstorming/writing-plans suggests review.","headings":["Stress Test: Adversarial Design Interrogation","Purpose","When to Invoke","The Process","Create a stress-test bead","Phase 1: Understand the Target","Phase 2: Map the Decision Tree","Phase 3: Interrogate One Branch at a Time","Phase 4: Document Findings","Stress Test Results: <topic>","Resolved Decisions","Changes Made","Deferred / Parking Lot","Confidence Assessment","Open in user's preferred editor, with platform fallbacks","If none available: just report the path","Phase 4.5: Reflexion Self-Review","Phase 5: Close"],"name_hint":"stress · 测试","description_zh":"在实施设计、计划或决策前进行对抗式审查，逐一追问决策树分支、提供建议答案，并要求明确认可或反驳。"},{"path":"skills/subagent-driven-development/SKILL.md","name":"subagent-driven-development","description":"Use when executing implementation plans with independent tasks in the current session","headings":["Subagent-Driven Development","When to Use","Pre-Flight Plan Review","The Process (Sequential Mode)","Parallel Batch Mode","Before you fan out (orchestrator-only)","Batch Execution Flow","Parallel Batch Walkthrough","Failed Task Handling","Mode Selection","Model Selection","Handling Reviewer ⚠️ Items","Fix Rounds","The Breaker","Final Review","File Handoffs","Prompt Templates","Example Workflow"],"name_hint":"subagent · driven · development","description_zh":"在当前会话执行由独立任务组成的实现计划，使用子智能体分别完成任务。"},{"path":"skills/systematic-debugging/SKILL.md","name":"systematic-debugging","description":"Use when encountering any bug, test failure, or unexpected behavior, before proposing fixes","headings":["Systematic Debugging","Overview","The Iron Law","When to Use","The Four Phases","Phase 1: Root Cause Investigation","Phase 2: Pattern Analysis","Phase 3: Hypothesis and Testing","Phase 4: Implementation","Red Flags - STOP and Follow Process","your human partner's Signals You're Doing It Wrong","Common Rationalizations","Quick Reference","When Process Reveals \"No Root Cause\"","Supporting Techniques","Integration"],"name_hint":"systematic · debugging","description_zh":"遇到缺陷、测试失败或意外行为时，先系统诊断问题，再提出修复。"},{"path":"skills/test-driven-development/SKILL.md","name":"test-driven-development","description":"Use when implementing any feature or bugfix, before writing implementation code","headings":["Test-Driven Development (TDD)","Overview","When to Use","The Iron Law","Red-Green-Refactor","RED - Write Failing Test","Verify RED - Watch It Fail","GREEN - Minimal Code","Verify GREEN - Watch It Pass","REFACTOR - Clean Up","Repeat","Good Tests","Common Rationalizations","Red Flags - STOP and Start Over","Example: Bug Fix","Verification Checklist","When Stuck","Debugging Integration"],"name_hint":"测试 · driven · development","description_zh":"在实现功能或修复缺陷前编写测试，按测试驱动流程开发实现代码。"},{"path":"skills/using-git-worktrees/SKILL.md","name":"using-git-worktrees","description":"Use when starting feature work that needs isolation from current workspace or before executing implementation plans - creates isolated git worktrees with smart directory selection and safety verification","headings":["Using Git Worktrees","Overview","Iron Law: Use `bd worktree`, NOT `git worktree`","Directory Selection","Safety Verification","Pre-Flight Checks","Detect Existing Worktree Isolation","Submodule Guard","Consent Flow","Creation Steps","0. Claim the bead first","1. Create Worktree with `bd worktree create`","Standard — creates worktree at .worktrees/<name> with matching branch","With explicit branch name","Then cd into it","2. Run Project Setup","Node.js","Rust"],"name_hint":"using · Git · worktrees","description_zh":"为需要隔离的功能或实施计划创建 Git worktree，选择合适目录并进行安全核验。"},{"path":"skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md","name":"using-superpowers","description":"Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions","headings":["The Rule","Skill Priority","Red Flags","Production-Grade Doctrine","Capturing Decisions","Beads","Skill Name Resolution","Platform Adaptation","Asking the User","User Instructions"],"name_hint":"using · superpowers","description_zh":"作为 Superpowers 的会话入口，介绍如何发现和调用 skill；作者要求任何回